[88] "Oddballs" are late 90s poly shroud masks that do not derive from the original sculpt. They get their name (not only for their odd faces) but because late 90s masks are always stamped with the parent company "Easter Unlimited Inc". It's peculiar that these sculpts ended up with a Fun World Div stamp and share no relation with the four early mask types covered in our guide. They are not featured in a Scream film and are significantly less sought after.

[89] Oddball masks featured a purple 'bat & moon' style header tag with Scream branding (nicknamed "ASIS" for As Seen in Scream).

[90] *Oddball masks have been found as #S9206 Glow-in-Dark Scream Masks with Shroud.